  "reconstructibility": 2,
  "reason": "The records collectively make the later study plausibly reconstructible. R2 supplies temperature-dependent MD mechanical testing of the same FeNiCrCoCu alloy and an HEA-coated metal matrix. R12 and R15 establish elevated-temperature tribological testing of HEA coatings, while R8 reports that heat exposure near 700–900 °C reduces coating hardness and worsens wear behavior. R1 links lattice disorder or amorphization to reduced modulus and strength in a closely related FCC HEA, and R3 and R16 identify HCP/stacking-fault and dislocation-mediated deformation in similar FCC multicomponent alloys. Although no single record contains the exact Cu-supported nanoscale coating, indentation protocol, full 300–1200 K range, and disorder-to-friction sequence, an expert could combine the same-alloy MD evidence, elevated-temperature coating tribology, and established disorder/dislocation mechanisms to propose the later intervention and mechanism."
